Vikram and Betal: The Lost Ring (Raw Story)

id: WBX_100127

King Vikram was carrying Betal through the forest once again.

Betal began his story.

“Once there was a man who lost his precious ring,” said Betal. “He searched everywhere but could not find it.”

He went to the king and asked for help.

The king called all the servants and said, “The person who has taken the ring should return it.”

No one spoke.

A wise minister stepped forward and said, “I have a way to find the thief.”

He gave each servant a flower and said, “The flower of the thief will bloom by tomorrow.”

All the servants took their flowers home.

The thief became scared and did not sleep all night.

The next day, all flowers looked the same.

But the minister noticed one servant looked very nervous.

He pointed at him and said, “You are the thief.”

The servant confessed.

Betal then asked, “Vikram, how did the minister know?”

Vikram replied, “Because fear made the thief behave differently.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

Fear reveals the truth.
